@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Manifest";
}

<div class="container mt-5">
    <div class="bg-lyra-dark text-light p-5 rounded shadow-sm">
        <h1 class="mb-4 fw-bold">
            <i class="bi bi-eye-slash-fill me-2"></i> Privacy Manifest
        </h1>

        <p class="text-light-emphasis fs-5 mb-4">
            In LYRA, privacy isn't a feature — it's a principle. Verification happens without inspection. Trust is explicit. Data stays yours.
        </p>

        <hr class="border-secondary" />

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-shield-shaded me-2 text-light"></i> What LYRA Sees
        </h5>
        <ul class="text-light-emphasis">
            <li>Canonical metadata: system names, method, path, timestamp</li>
            <li>Payload hashes — not raw request bodies</li>
            <li>Access permissions between systems via policies</li>
            <li>Cryptographic signatures and verification results</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-eye me-2 text-light"></i> What LYRA Ignores
        </h5>
        <ul class="text-light-emphasis">
            <li>No access to user data, cookies, sessions, or headers</li>
            <li>No inspection of payload content beyond hash validation</li>
            <li>No storage of dynamic secrets or API tokens</li>
            <li>No tracking, profiling, or external reporting</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-link-45deg me-2 text-light"></i> Trust is Defined
        </h5>
        <p class="text-light-emphasis">
            LYRA enforces trust through precise, bidirectional policies. No defaults. No assumptions. Each call is verified.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-in-right me-2 text-light"></i> Yours to Host
        </h5>
        <p class="text-light-emphasis">
            LYRA runs entirely within <span class="fw-bold text-light">your environment</span>. No cloud sync. No dependencies. No external authorities.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-shield-lock me-2 text-light"></i> Signed. Checked. Done.
        </h5>
        <p class="text-light-emphasis">
            Every request must be signed. Every signature is verified. Deterministic. Reproducible. Secure.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-person-lines-fill me-2 text-light"></i> Maintained By
        </h5>
        <p class="text-light-emphasis">
            Built and maintained by <strong>Yurii Pasternak</strong> (<a href="mailto:pasternak2048@gmail.com" class="text-info">pasternak2048@gmail.com</a>).<br />
            Source available on <a href="https://github.com/pasternak2048" class="text-info" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
        </p>

        <hr class="border-secondary" />

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4">
            <i class="bi bi-shield-check me-2 text-light"></i> Privacy by Architecture
        </h5>
        <p class="text-light-emphasis">
            LYRA is designed for zero-trust systems: clean boundaries, no overreach, clear contracts. Security through clarity.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>